I won't post the whole ascension tale from my latest wizard (it's my 3rd 
wizard ascension, but I never get tired of wizards). However, what I did 
  to a storekeeper was quite devious.

After finding a nice magic marker with 90 charges in it I decided to 
write a spellbook of polymorph. No problem, given I was extremely lucky. 
Unfortunately, my skills in matter spells was lacking, so I ran around 
and cast wizard lock until I could enhance my matter skills.

Pretty soon, I was having all kinds of fun polymorphing things. I was on 
the minetown level, and I decided, what the heck - I'll see what happens 
if I polypile the items in the hardware store on the level.

Predictable, the storekeeper became unreasonably angry and started 
zapping a wand of striking. I wanted to simply kill him, but my 
intrinsic AC was down to 1 after donating piles of gold to the priests. 
I didn't want to risk upsetting the gods and losing my AC.

So I polymorphed him into a lemure, left the shop, and wizard locked his 
door shut so he couldn't escape. I bought my candles fair and square, 
and left the storekeeper to stew in his shop over his poor choice of 
customer service.

